---
import Analytics from '../components/Analytics.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import SiteBar from '../components/SiteBar.astro'
import { siteRoot } from '../home/paths'
import '../theme.css'
import '../home/site.css'
import '../home/footer.css'

// Two services and what each one is for. Short on purpose.
const REPO = 'https://github.com/cmdcolin/bender'
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${siteRoot}favicon.svg`} />
    <title>Privacy — bender</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="bender uses Google Analytics to count visits and Firebase to store your saved voices. Nothing else."
    />
    <Analytics />
  </head>
  <body id="top">
    <SiteBar account={false} />

    <main class="wrap privacy">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="privacyLead">
        bender runs in your browser. Two outside services are involved, and this
        page is the whole list.
      </p>

      <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Counts visits: which pages get opened, roughly where from, and on what
        sort of device. It sets cookies to do that. Any tracker blocker switches
        it off, and everything here works the same without it.
      </p>

      <h2>Firebase</h2>
      <p>
        Only if you sign in. Google handles the sign-in, and one Firestore
        document holds your saved voices: a name, and the board it stands for,
        spelled the same way a shared link spells it. The same document holds
        the board you last had open, so the home page can offer it back. Stay
        signed out and there is no document at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting rid of it</h2>
      <p>
        <b>×</b> in the saved menu deletes a voice on the spot. To have the
        whole document deleted, say so in
        <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>an issue</a>. Nothing is sold and there are
        no ads.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
